  "notes": "Used almost exclusively for negative things being uncovered — scandals, fraud, lies, secrets. Typically used with する to form a verb meaning 'to be exposed/come to light.'\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {不正|ふせい}が{露見|ろけん}する: fraud/wrongdoing is exposed\n- {嘘|うそ}が{露見|ろけん}する: a lie comes to light\n- {秘密|ひみつ}が{露見|ろけん}する: a secret is revealed\n- {犯行|はんこう}が{露見|ろけん}する: a crime is discovered\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {発覚|はっかく}: discovery, detection — very similar; also used for negative things being uncovered; slightly more common in news\n- {暴露|ばくろ}: exposure, revelation — implies someone actively reveals information, often whistleblowing\n- {判明|はんめい}: becoming clear — neutral; used for any fact becoming known, not just negative ones",
